outside the study area); a record with no valid position stays where it
was (\code{jitter_failed}). Records with an uncertainty of 0 do not move;
records without one move by \code{na_uncertainty} metres, or stay fixed when
it is \code{NA}.

\strong{Is it worth it?} For each record, the range of each layer over the
replicates is divided by the species' niche breadth on that layer (the
distance between the \code{breadth_probs} quantiles of the values at the
records), the same scale as \code{\link[=uncertainty_environment]{uncertainty_environment()}}. Records whose
environment changes by more than \code{max_rel} of the breadth are the ones
that make propagating worth the extra model runs; when there are almost
none, the replicates are environmentally the same dataset.

\strong{Link with \code{\link[=uncertainty_environment]{uncertainty_environment()}}.} Both measure how much the
